"""
Investment import service for all supported brokers.

Code version: v0.105.0
- Added: Broker snapshot payloads now expose per-account and per-ticker
  realized-P&L coverage, independent as-of dates, and replay requirements so
  consumers cannot treat a partial performance boundary as complete.
- Fixed: HSBC non-USD cash-only refreshes now retain the authoritative current
  USD cash boundary from the existing ledger, so the merged multi-currency
  snapshot remains eligible for current total-equity calculations.
- Changed: Futu (HK) monthly statement PDFs now use the shared bounded CPU
  process pool for independent file parsing, preserving upload order and
  falling back safely when process execution is unavailable.
- Changed: IBKR Web paste can now parse a full Your Holdings clipboard
  capture into its optional cash and position boundary, preserving the raw
  snapshot as immutable source evidence and rejecting account mismatches.
- Fixed: Schwab date-only same-day buy and sell rows now follow the
  export's source chronology instead of cash-safety ordering; an explicit
  user-confirmed sequence remains authoritative across re-imports.
- Fixed: Incremental Schwab imports now canonicalize legacy persisted
  `nra_tax_adj` withholding rows before duplicate matching, while retaining the
  original stored type as source provenance instead of double-counting tax.
- Fixed: Schwab dividend exports now classify `NRA Tax Adj` and related
  withholding-tax actions as `foreign_tax_withholding` instead of preserving
  them as unknown transaction types.
- Fixed: Schwab CSV imports now distinguish date-only rows from genuine
  intraday timestamps and prefer an explicit datetime field when one exists.
- Fixed: Schwab numeric parsing now accepts accounting-style parenthetical
  negatives and Unicode minus signs used by statement exports.
- Fixed: HSBC current cash now uses the captured ledger balance as the posted
  cash boundary, applies pending settlements exactly once, and preserves the
  bank's available balance as separate audit evidence.
- Fixed: Legacy HSBC ledgers can conservatively recover a missing current
  ledger balance from same-date, account-matched settlement postings.
- Added: A standalone HSBC USD Savings cash refresh can be imported after
  settlement without replacing the existing Portfolio position snapshot.
- Fixed: USD cash-only settlement refreshes retain hidden `REF P... SEC`
  rows as evidence and reconcile them back into existing HSBC orders, so
  pending buys are cleared only after the bank has posted their cash legs.
- Changed: User-specific broker performance and tax-lot evidence is loaded only
  from the ignored device-local settings store instead of source control.
- Changed: HSBC execution-notification timestamp reconciliation can refresh
  prior email-derived Asia/Shanghai notification timestamps when a verified
  Gmail message provides the canonical America/New_York proxy.
- Changed: HSBC execution-notification timestamp reconciliation now permits
  timestamp-only evidence when the email body omits a price or the settled
  order price has been normalized separately; order identity, direction,
  ticker, and total quantity remain required.
- Fixed: HSBC cash boundaries from a newer incremental paste now survive an
  older Portfolio snapshot winning the position merge, keeping current cash
  and pending-settlement estimates aligned with the latest USD Savings page.
- Fixed: Schwab paired Journal cleanup rows are now identified from the
  imported Security Transfer evidence instead of a date- and account-suffix-
  specific six-row allowlist. Existing stale cleanup rows are removed when a
  later authoritative Schwab bundle is re-imported, while source artifacts
  remain immutable evidence.
- Fixed: HSBC settled-order cash balances now use the final chronological
  principal or fee posting instead of an intermediate fee balance.
- Fixed: Authoritative HSBC USD Savings Transaction History CSV evidence now
  repairs same-day copy/paste row-order conflicts for matched settled orders.
- Fixed: IBKR same-day position snapshots now compare the precise observed
  snapshot time before falling back to row completeness, so an older manual
  capture cannot override a later official file snapshot.
- Fixed: IBKR broker summaries now mirror the selected cumulative CSV
  performance snapshot instead of retaining a conflicting closed-trade subset.
- Fixed: HSBC pending-settlement cash summaries now use the authoritative
  base-currency cash boundary when one is available, while retaining the raw
  USD Savings balance separately for auditability.
- Changed: Unposted, source-labelled pending-settlement fee evidence remains
  auditable metadata but is no longer deducted from current display cash;
  only a settled cash posting can apply the fee to the balance.
- Fixed: IBKR realized-performance snapshots now retain an incomplete CSV
  aggregate, merge adjacent non-overlapping statement periods, and avoid
  replacing cumulative P&L with one latest-window closed-trade subset.
- Changed: HSBC pending-settlement cash summaries now apply the signed net
  amount of visible unsettled buy and sell orders, so the current display
  estimate includes pending buys as well as pending sells. Unposted sell
  clearing fees and other settlement adjustments remain explicitly unknown.
- Fixed: One Trade Notifications paste may now contain current-day filled rows
  whose display omits the date alongside older rows that retain full dates.
  The user-selected Hong Kong page date applies only to the time-only rows;
  dated historical rows keep their own displayed dates.
- Fixed: Immutable IBKR GainsKeeper split fills now replace one matching
  provisional compact web aggregate when account, trade identity, split
  count, signed quantity, and gross value close exactly; GainsKeeper retains
  its authoritative commission and net-cash precision.
- Added: GainsKeeper-reported IBKR cash balances now retain authoritative
  statement-period dates, allowing a newer file snapshot to supersede an
  older user-entered web cash boundary without carrying stale intraday tags.
- Fixed: IBKR GainsKeeper cash boundaries now retain the latest intraday
  transaction time, so the final imported fill receives the reported cash
  balance instead of a stale pre-fill replay value.
- Fixed: IBKR GainsKeeper imports now retain BUYOTHER and SELLOTHER money-market
  transactions with their original FITIDs, exact timestamps, and cash values.
- Fixed: Legacy IBKR GainsKeeper rows are normalized back to the source's
  America/New_York timestamp, and exact FITIDs now deduplicate across date and
  time representations during incremental merges.
- Fixed: User-confirmed current-cash scope and the HSBC effective cash boundary
  now survive incremental imports from another broker without being replaced
  by historical transaction replay balances.
- Fixed: An IBKR compact Orders aggregate with complete same-page fill
  details now supersedes only an exactly reconciling full-page split-fill
  representation, preventing an aggregate order and its constituent fills
  from both entering the local ledger.
- Fixed: IBKR full Trade Notifications captures retain same-minute split fills
  instead of dropping a second fill that shares the account, side, ticker,
  quantity, price, and venue with the first fill.
- Added: IBKR web-paste imports can retain a user-entered position snapshot at
  its exact cash boundary without creating synthetic transactions or applying
  account-specific calibration to later captures.
- Fixed: IBKR Trade Notifications are explicitly recorded as supplemental
  transaction evidence after a file-snapshot cutoff. Their unique fills are
  additive, while matching CSV or GainsKeeper rows refine the provisional
  web row instead of treating the paste as a replacement snapshot.
- Added: IBKR web-paste imports can retain an exact user-verified post-fill
  cash balance as a dated, intraday cash boundary without creating a synthetic
  transaction.
- Fixed: A newer IBKR user-verified cash boundary cannot be rolled back by an
  older GainsKeeper or Transaction History snapshot during a later merge.
- Fixed: IBKR compact Orders captures now reconcile same-page split Trades
  details, so a filled order can retain its aggregate fee without importing
  duplicate partial fills or fabricating a zero commission.
- Added: IBKR's compact Orders page cards are accepted as provisional
  Trade Notifications evidence when the caller supplies the displayed Hong
  Kong page date. Missing fee lines remain explicitly unknown and are never
  converted into a fabricated zero commission.
- Fixed: HSBC snapshot and coverage metadata now merge monotonically, so an
  older re-import or mixed-ledger merge cannot roll back a newer verified
  tax-lot boundary.
- Fixed: HSBC authoritative Portfolio snapshots now extend an existing
  verified tax-lot boundary through a fully covered incremental Order Status
  window when the projected ending shares match the snapshot exactly.
- Fixed: Incremental IBKR CSV imports no longer let a latest-window
  Realized Summary value of zero overwrite exact historical GainsKeeper
  closed-trade realized P&L retained in the merged ledger.
- Fixed: IBKR CSV cash snapshots retain both their reported statement date and
  the last transaction date available for cash replay, so a statement ending
  one calendar day after its last trade still anchors current cash correctly.
- Fixed: Legacy paired HSBC PDF statements reconcile closing holdings from the
  printed opening quantities plus the statement-period trades, retain charges
  that cross a PDF page boundary, and expose complete multi-currency cash and
  transaction-date metadata.
- Fixed: A later authoritative HSBC statement snapshot can advance an older
  copy/paste snapshot, while an older statement still cannot roll back newer
  live cash or position evidence.
- Fixed: HSBC statement imports preserve explicit zero balances, reject printed
  balance discontinuities, expose transaction coverage dates, and union
  historical statement metadata across incremental imports.
- Fixed: A newer IBKR GainsKeeper position snapshot can extend a verified cost
  basis through exact post-snapshot GainsKeeper buys when the source window,
  FITIDs, quantities, and commission-inclusive net costs close completely.
  Unexplained share changes still discard stale basis evidence.
- Fixed: An attributed positive HSBC `CORP EVT PAYMENT` retains or repairs its
  dividend classification when a less-specific cash row is merged later, while
  matching paste and CSV rows reconcile as one event. Recurring SGOV
  distributions can no longer be downgraded to deposits, duplicated across
  source formats, or omitted from realized P&L.
- Fixed: User-verified open HSBC DRAM and EUV tax-lot histories retain their
  reconstructed realized P&L when exact trade counts, quantities, and ending
  shares agree with the authoritative 7 Aug 2026 position snapshot.
- Fixed: Manual internal-transfer v3 keys survive additive source-evidence
  enrichment, such as a statement SHA-256 added after the original binding.
  Duplicate same-value rows still require their immutable row identity and
  ambiguous historical keys remain fail-closed.
- Added: HSBC statement PDF imports retain every exact source file as immutable
  evidence and link each parsed or enriched cash row to its SHA-256 digest.
- Added: HSBC settled orders expose any exact difference between gross plus
  commission and the authoritative bank settlement as an auditable settlement
  adjustment instead of leaving the residual implicit.
- Fixed: Longbridge (HK) paired-file reconciliation zeros are explicitly
  non-authoritative cash snapshots and cannot reset a real cash balance.
- Added: DKIM-authenticated HSBC execution-notification timestamps can replace
  the date-only Order Status fallback after the order ID, side, ticker,
  quantity, price, and New York trade date all agree. The retained provenance
  makes clear that this is the bank's notification time, not a venue fill
  report, and survives a later three-page HSBC re-import.
- Fixed: HSBC date-only Order Status executions now retain the page's
  newest-first source rank as their immutable same-day execution order. SEC
  cash-posting rows remain cash evidence and can no longer reorder buys and
  sells or manufacture a transient short position during replay.
- Added: HSBC orders retain every matched SEC cash posting, including
  interleaved fee legs and their source-ledger sequence, so the frontend can
  replay confirmed settlement cash without synthesizing transaction rows.
- Fixed: Incremental imports index stable duplicate candidates instead of
  scanning the entire historical ledger for every existing record.
- Added: Longbridge paired-file imports retain exact Fund Details and History
  Orders source artifacts, while user-confirmed broker P&L calibrations remain
  explicitly distinguishable from a future broker-native performance report.
- Fixed: HSBC same-day Portfolio evidence now uses the page's explicit market-data update time, so a newer paste cannot be shadowed by an older same-date snapshot.
- Fixed: IBKR GainsKeeper position evidence no longer inherits an older CSV
  cost basis when the authoritative quantity has changed; same-date evidence
  with verified cost-basis fields is preferred during idempotent re-imports.
- Fixed: IBKR base-currency-equivalent cash funding may settle at an eligible
  bank one calendar day after the broker posting, including HKD and CNH bank
  legs, while longer or unrelated future outflows remain rejected.
- Fixed: Exact duplicate HSBC cash rows from one source row now merge into one
  ledger event instead of creating an ambiguous internal-transfer key.
- Added: IBKR GainsKeeper OFX/GKX security-transfer rows are retained as zero-cash transfer legs and upgrade matching legacy transfer records with FITID and unit-price evidence.
- Added: newer IBKR GainsKeeper position snapshots retain authoritative cost-basis fields from the existing IBKR open-positions CSV while adding current market values and prices.
- Added: IBKR Transaction History base-currency-equivalent cash rows can be manually bound to CNH bank withdrawals without mistaking the raw CNH amount for USD.
- Added: CMB Wing Lung bank-side cash deposits are valid manual counterparts for Futu (HK) cash withdrawals.
- Fixed: HSBC broker summaries preserve the account-level Portfolio snapshot and
  pending-settlement cash boundary after mixed-broker merges, so the frontend can
  distinguish current source evidence from an incomplete order replay.
- Fixed: IBKR Realized Summary foreign-currency cash flows now replace their
  base-currency Transaction History equivalents, so CNH/CNY deposit and
  withdrawal legs remain available for exact internal-transfer binding.
- Fixed: Futu (HK) transfers from the HK Stocks Account are retained in the Futu cash ledger but excluded from external-funding aggregation without fabricating a missing source leg.
- Fixed: HSBC manual current-cash calibration is preserved when an older USD history import cannot replace the newer component snapshot.
- Fixed: Schwab's paired post-transfer Journal rows are suppressed without
  removing the paired Security Transfer receipts, so bound cross-broker source
  legs remain reconciled with their visible receipts.
- Changed: Schwab cleanup detection now requires balanced positive and negative
  Journal quantities plus a matching Security Transfer receipt in the same
  account and ticker scope. Unpaired Journal rows remain in the ledger for
  review rather than being guessed away.
- Changed: BOCHK statement imports now canonicalize printed CNY/RMB to CNH, retain the printed currency as source provenance, preserve HKD Current versus HKD Savings identity, and migrate prior CNY internal-transfer binding keys.
- Fixed: Schwab Positions `Incomplete` cost-basis sentinels are treated as unavailable rather than malformed numeric input.
- Added: Users can persist a reversible ignore decision for false-positive internal-transfer source candidates without changing the underlying transaction or cash replay.
- Fixed: Mixed-store HSBC non-USD cash imports merge into existing per-currency snapshots without regressing a newer USD calibration.
- Fixed: HSBC cash summaries in mixed-broker stores now preserve the latest balance for every cash subaccount instead of inferring one broker balance from the last transaction globally.
- Added: HSBC USD Savings Transaction History CSV calibration validates balance continuity and records the latest USD Savings balance as authoritative source evidence.
- Changed: HSBC copy/paste cash snapshots now fail closed on malformed subaccount sections, retain the newest per-subaccount balance when duplicate or historical clips are merged, and avoid double-counting legacy statement currency totals beside explicit subaccount balances.
- Fixed: Manual cross-broker security-transfer bindings require exact same-day source and receipt evidence, so the legacy binding API cannot bypass Schwab's fail-closed reconciliation.
"""

